.TH "VTTREGION.LINES" "3JS" "June 18, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
VTTRegion.lines \- VTTRegion: lines property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]lines\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R]
interface represents the height of the region, in number of lines.
.SH VALUE
A number representing the number of lines inside the region that cue
text is rendered in.
The default is \f[CR]3\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
In the following example, a new \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] is created, then
the value of \f[CR]lines\f[R] is set to \f[CR]4\f[R].
The value is then printed to the console.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] region = \f[B]new\f[R] VTTRegion();
region.lines = 4; \f[I]// Render cues in 4 lines\f[R]
console.log(region.lines);
.EE
